78 #edb/ref 17592186319833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320257 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2a5d0bf9-0555-588a-8937-9468b4e30755" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186320010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186319609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320450 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8c4879d1-521b-5d88-bd53-72f2ed650b99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35316" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da3efbc4-2fa4-54a8-9aa9-e1c2c723490a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1074 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
